# Dynamic Task Resolution Refactor

## 🎯 Problem

- `ITaskProcessor<TTask, TResult>` is generic and resolved at compile time
- Dependency Injection cannot resolve processors from runtime `Task` types
- Conditional execution requires runtime task dispatch
- Current design cannot dynamically execute `TrueTask / FalseTask`

---

## ✅ Goal

Introduce a **non-generic registry-based execution system** that:

- Resolves `Task → Processor` at runtime
- Keeps processors strongly typed internally
- Removes DI generic resolution dependency
- Enables clean conditional + workflow execution

---

## 🛠️ TODO

### 1. Introduce non-generic processor abstraction
- [ ] Create `ITaskProcessor`
- [ ] Expose `Type TaskType`
- [ ] Add `object Execute(Task task)`

---

### 2. Create typed base processor
- [ ] Implement `TaskProcessor<TTask, TResult>`
- [ ] Handle casting internally
- [ ] Preserve strong typing in concrete implementations

---

### 3. Migrate existing processors
- [ ] Convert all processors to inherit `TaskProcessor<T, R>`
- [ ] Remove direct generic DI resolution usage

---

### 4. Build registry layer
- [ ] Create `TaskProcessorRegistry`
- [ ] Inject `IEnumerable<ITaskProcessor>`
- [ ] Map `Dictionary<Type, ITaskProcessor>`
- [ ] Resolve processor via runtime `Task.GetType()`

---

### 5. Add execution boundary
- [ ] Create `ITaskExecutor`
- [ ] Use registry to resolve processor
- [ ] Execute task dynamically at runtime

---

### 6. Fix conditional flow
- [ ] Conditional processor only selects next task
- [ ] Do NOT execute nested tasks inside processors
- [ ] Executor handles continuation

---

## 🧠 Mindmap

                     ┌────────────────────┐
                     │       Task         │
                     │   (pure data)      │
                     └─────────┬──────────┘
                               │
                               ▼
             ┌──────────────────────────────┐
             │    TaskProcessorRegistry     │
             │  Type → Processor mapping    │
             └─────────┬────────────────────┘
                       │
                       ▼
             ┌──────────────────────┐
             │     TaskExecutor     │
             │ (runtime dispatcher) │
             └─────────┬────────────┘
                       │
        ┌──────────────┴──────────────┐
        ▼                             ▼
┌────────────────┐        ┌──────────────────┐
│ Conditional     │        │ Addition Task    │
│ Processor       │        │ Processor        │
└──────┬──────────┘        └────────┬─────────┘
       │                            │
       ▼                            ▼
  select branch              execute logic
       │
       ▼
 TrueTask / FalseTask
       │
       ▼
 Executor continues workflow

---

## 🧭 Core Insight

- DI resolves known types only
- Runtime execution requires type dispatch
- Therefore a registry layer is required
- Processors must NOT execute other tasks directly
